  "role": "adjudicator",
  "task_id": "LEV-CH01-FINITE-VOLUME-CELL-AVERAGE-CANONICAL-20260908",
  "trigger": [
    "judge classifications differ",
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
    "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D025 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The disagreement concerns evidentiary sufficiency, not two demonstrated interpretations of the averaging formula. The direct judgment identifies the selected measure with Lebesgue measure by invoking the library trust boundary; the supplied declaration does not expose that identification. The supported classification is undetermined, rather than either established equivalence or established mismatch.",
      "primary_evidence": "D025 supplies only the type MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace Real and body inferInstance. D009 projects its measure. D003 normalizes the resulting integral by right - left. Printed page 5, Section 1.2 requires normalization of the spatial cell integral by geometric cell volume."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The request is justified. Independent comparison of the direct and blind dossiers finds the same unresolved measure instance in both. Neither the complete local imported source nor the reuse ledger supplies its resolved construction or interval normalization.",
      "primary_evidence": "Both dossiers display D025 as inferInstance with semantic SHA256 d9de6598dfa4dc9b2cc1dfbccf206b37d159db61f4b35cc745a68902fbc74b22. The reuse ledger contains no D025 interpretation. The local averaging definition uses volume without establishing its normalization."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Undetermined remains appropriate under the supplied evidence restrictions. All identified substantive uncertainty is concentrated in the measure bridge and its consequences. No evidence establishes that the actual Lean measure is incorrect.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 4, equation (1.10) supplies spatial integration dx. D003 and D060 supply integration against the measure projected from D025, whose displayed body does not identify its resolved value."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D025 unclear",
      "resolution": "D025 determines a fixed measure-space instance, not a universally quantified arbitrary measure. Nevertheless, its particular measure and normalization cannot be independently recovered from inferInstance. Its module ownership and name indicate intended library provenance but do not resolve the disputed semantic content. This dependency remains unclear.",
      "primary_evidence": "The fully explicit target uses @MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume Real Real.measureSpace. D009 returns self.2; D025 displays no instance argument or resolved construction beyond inferInstance."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Strictly ordered finite real endpoints appropriately express a positive-length interval. Local integrability imposes no continuity, differentiability, global integrability, PDE, or uniform-grid condition. These are appropriate analytic explications if the selected measure is spatial Lebesgue measure. The effective integrability domain remains conditional on resolving D025.",
      "primary_evidence": "D007 requires IntegrableOn on (left,right] and (right,left]; the latter is empty under left < right. Printed page 5 motivates the definition with discontinuous solutions and supplies no smoothness requirement."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "The structural conclusion is complete: the candidate is the exact integral over the selected interval multiplied by the reciprocal of that interval's positive length. No numerical update or approximation estimate belongs to the selected definition. Certification that this numerator is the source spatial integral remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 requires equality with D003; D002 is an abbreviation of D003; D003 uses the same state and endpoints in integration and normalization. Printed page 5 defines the exact cell average and separately describes its approximation."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The supplied bodies establish conjunction, exact equality, the candidate abbreviation, interval orientation, endpoint subtraction, reciprocal, and real vector scalar normalization. Reused algebraic and topological projections preserve the structures instantiated in this target; their hashes do not certify the averaging measure. D025 remains the material unresolved operator dependency.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001-D003, D007, D018, D032-D033, D041-D042, D047-D050, D052-D053, and D055-D060 expose the relevant operations. D016-D019 supply finite-product structures; the remaining supplied structure conversions do not introduce an alternate averaging operator. D009 and D025 leave the concrete measure bridge unexposed."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Zero and reversed widths are excluded, so the theorem does not rely on totalized inversion at zero. The reverse integration interval is empty. However, equivalence between half-open and other endpoint conventions requires null endpoints for the selected measure, which is not established by the displayed D025 declaration.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target assumes left < right. D003 inverts right - left. D060 integrates over Set.Ioc left right minus Set.Ioc right left. The source supplies no degenerate-cell convention or alternative atomic spatial measure."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The finite real-vector codomain presents no incomplete-space obstruction, and positive width plus the stated integrability premise provides the ordinary analytic conditions for the selected integral. No PDE existence or uniqueness claim is required. Matching these conditions to spatial averaging remains unresolved solely through the measure identification.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target codomain is Fin m → Real with the supplied finite-product normed structures; D024 includes real completeness. D007 states local integrability. Printed pages 4-5 motivate the averaging operation through spatial conservation laws without making PDE solvability a prerequisite for its definition."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The semantic implication is conditional on identifying the selected measure with correctly normalized spatial measure. After that identification, choose state x = q(x,t) and the ordered endpoints of any interval cell; the normalized integral is precisely the source average. Without it, the displayed operation has not been shown to recover the source quantity.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 1 permits finite real-vector states; printed page 4 fixes spatial integration at a given time; printed page 5 defines the normalized cell integral. D003 divides the D025-measure integral by geometric width rather than explicitly dividing by the selected measure's cell mass."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "With the measure bridge established, the source definition supplies the constructed normalized integral and D001 merely packages its equality with the already assumed admissibility conditions. The reflexivity of the expanded Lean proposition alone cannot certify that the defined object represents the source average. The semantic implication remains unclear.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 unfolds to D003, and D001 therefore adds A = A to the two premises. The source defines a particular spatial average, so matching the meaning of A requires the unresolved D025 identification."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity, applicability, and ancillary checklist consistency",
      "resolution": "The premises are satisfiable in positive dimension: a zero state on endpoints 0 and 1 is integrable for the selected measure. Thus validity does not depend on m = 0 or impossible premises. Definitional reflexivity is appropriate for this source definition but cannot establish measure correctness. Universal state and endpoint binders preserve fixed-time slices, all finite real component counts, and nonuniform interval cells. The empty-vector extension supplies no substantive stronger result. N01 is best marked not-applicable because the selected claim is a definition; the round-trip pass expresses the compatible observation that cell locality is retained.",
      "primary_evidence": "The elaborated target universally quantifies m, state, left, and right. D001-D003 show definitional packaging; D004-D005 and D010 include positive dimensions as well as zero. Printed page 5 selects a local averaging definition, with flux updates discussed separately."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "The vector type, local interval, fixed-time interpretation, exact-value role, and reciprocal-width normalization match the selected source definition. Recovering the spatial cell integral additionally requires establishing that the fixed measure extracted from D025 is ordinary Lebesgue measure with interval mass right - left. The supplied declaration and reuse evidence do not establish this disputed bridge. Equivalence would follow upon resolving it; no actual counterexample to the target's measure identification has been established."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the intended Lebesgue-measure identification, the source definition yields the normalized integral and the remaining conclusion conjuncts repeat the target premises. As a bare logical proposition, the unfolded target is reflexive regardless of the averaging operator; that observation does not establish semantic representation of the source-defined object. The evidence leaves that representation unresolved through D025."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The supplied D025 body does not expose the resolved Real.measureSpace instance or establish that its projected measure is Lebesgue measure normalized by interval length. Consequently, matching the numerator, effective integrability domain, and endpoint-null conventions remains conditional on that identification."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-integration-measure-evidence",
      "evidence": "D025 contains only inferInstance; D009 extracts its measure; D003 integrates against it but divides by right - left. Neither dossier nor the supplied reuse ledger establishes the selected measure's normalization. The primary source uses spatial integration dx and geometric cell volume.",
      "impact": "Acceptance cannot be certified from the allowed evidence. This is an unresolved evidence gap, not a demonstrated mathematical error. A resolved instance declaration and its spatial normalization evidence would address the common cause of the outstanding semantic checks."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "appropriate-definitional-packaging",
      "evidence": "D001-D003 expand the target into the two admissibility premises together with equality of the constructed normalized integral to itself. Printed page 5 selects the definition of the exact average.",
      "impact": "The theorem's definitional simplicity is not a faithfulness defect or evidence of impossible-premise vacuity. It also provides no independent verification of the disputed measure."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached primary-source pages and the inline declarations confirms the intended one-dimensional, finite real-vector, fixed-time normalized cell integral. The disputed dependency was rechecked in both dossiers and against the reuse ledger. Its displayed instance-inference placeholder does not resolve the specific measure normalization challenged by the blind translation and round-trip judgment. The direct judgment's library-boundary assumption supplies no additional declaration evidence for that disputed point. All other identified differences are appropriate definitional or analytic explications, with satisfiable hypotheses and no substantive claim of stronger applicability. Both semantic implication directions therefore remain unclear, requiring an undetermined classification and nonacceptance pending the missing evidence. Source-byte and rendering hashes were accepted as supplied and were not independently recomputed."
}
